values ('a5b6c7d8-9e0f-4a40-9d90-0b1c2d3e4f30', 'religious-ethics', 'Religious Ethics', 'Religious Ethics examines how religious traditions form moral persons and communities, interpret authoritative sources, reason about virtue, law, justice, care, violence, economics, bodies, technology, and public life, and deliberate across deep pluralism. Students learn to read primary sources, compare moral vocabularies carefully, analyze contested cases, and write arguments that are historically grounded, ethically rigorous, and publicly intelligible.');

